1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,266
What if the most advanced chip factory

2
00:00:03,266 --> 00:00:05,094
on Earth could be stopped,

3
00:00:05,094 --> 00:00:07,188
not by a broken machine,

4
00:00:07,188 --> 00:00:10,439
but by a missing bottle of liquid?

5
00:00:10,683 --> 00:00:12,792
It has almost happened,

6
00:00:12,792 --> 00:00:14,143
more than once.

7
00:00:14,143 --> 00:00:15,982
A chemical from Japan,

8
00:00:15,982 --> 00:00:17,356
a gas from Ukraine,

9
00:00:17,356 --> 00:00:19,353
a metal from China.

10
00:00:19,383 --> 00:00:20,008
Each time,

11
00:00:20,008 --> 00:00:22,378
the chip industry discovered that its

12
00:00:22,378 --> 00:00:24,317
weakest link was not a machine worth

13
00:00:24,317 --> 00:00:26,235
hundreds of millions of dollars,

14
00:00:26,235 --> 00:00:28,774
but something that fits in a truck.

15
00:00:39,417 --> 00:00:42,015
What is the most important chemical in

16
00:00:42,015 --> 00:00:43,797
a chip factory?

17
00:00:48,417 --> 00:00:52,227
A strong candidate is photoresist.

18
00:00:52,377 --> 00:00:54,510
It is a light-sensitive liquid spread

19
00:00:54,510 --> 00:00:56,817
across the silicon wafer.

20
00:00:56,987 --> 00:00:59,428
When the lithography machine shines its

21
00:00:59,428 --> 00:01:00,515
pattern of light,

22
00:01:00,515 --> 00:01:02,955
the resist changes wherever the light hits

23
00:01:02,955 --> 00:01:03,777
it.

24
00:01:03,917 --> 00:01:04,514
Wash it,

25
00:01:04,514 --> 00:01:06,573
and the circuit design is left behind

26
00:01:06,573 --> 00:01:07,582
on the wafer,

27
00:01:07,582 --> 00:01:09,417
ready to be etched.

28
00:01:09,547 --> 00:01:10,005
No resist,

29
00:01:10,005 --> 00:01:10,757
no pattern.

30
00:01:10,757 --> 00:01:12,066
No pattern,

31
00:01:12,066 --> 00:01:13,337
no chip.

32
00:01:13,583 --> 00:01:16,443
And resist is not a commodity.

33
00:01:16,623 --> 00:01:19,657
Every new generation of chips needs a

34
00:01:19,657 --> 00:01:20,644
new recipe,

35
00:01:20,644 --> 00:01:22,136
tuned to the light,

36
00:01:22,136 --> 00:01:24,664
the machine and the chemistry of one

37
00:01:24,664 --> 00:01:26,023
factory.

38
00:01:26,293 --> 00:01:28,813
That takes hundreds of test cycles between

39
00:01:28,813 --> 00:01:31,703
the resist maker and the chipmaker.

40
00:01:31,963 --> 00:01:33,957
One of the biggest suppliers says

41
00:01:33,957 --> 00:01:36,700
developing a new resist can take up

42
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:38,048
to two years.

43
00:01:38,283 --> 00:01:40,313
For the most advanced chips,

44
00:01:40,313 --> 00:01:42,857
made with extreme ultraviolet light,

45
00:01:42,857 --> 00:01:45,513
the market belongs to Japan.

46
00:01:45,883 --> 00:01:48,738
According to the research firm QYResearch,

47
00:01:48,738 --> 00:01:50,633
three Japanese companies,

48
00:01:50,633 --> 00:01:52,289
Tokyo Ohka Kogyo,

49
00:01:52,289 --> 00:01:54,424
JSR and Shin-Etsu Chemical,

50
00:01:54,424 --> 00:01:57,063
hold about ninety percent of the world

51
00:01:57,063 --> 00:01:58,663
market for EUV resist.

52
00:01:58,663 --> 00:02:00,663
It is an estimate.

53
00:02:00,733 --> 00:02:03,639
But it means the most advanced factories

54
00:02:03,639 --> 00:02:04,669
in Taiwan,

55
00:02:04,669 --> 00:02:07,840
Korea and America all depend on a

56
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:10,553
few chemical plants in Japan.

57
00:02:10,593 --> 00:02:12,625
And this resist sells for about one

58
00:02:12,625 --> 00:02:15,482
thousand eight hundred dollars a gallon.

59
00:02:15,717 --> 00:02:17,867
And the dependence grows with every

60
00:02:17,867 --> 00:02:19,327
generation.

61
00:02:19,387 --> 00:02:21,911
Moving from three nanometer chips to two

62
00:02:21,911 --> 00:02:24,205
nanometer chips adds more than thirty

63
00:02:24,205 --> 00:02:26,270
percent more layers printed with extreme

64
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:27,624
ultraviolet light,

65
00:02:27,624 --> 00:02:30,977
according to Korean industry figures.

66
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:32,598
Each layer needs its own coat of

67
00:02:32,598 --> 00:02:33,253
resist,

68
00:02:33,253 --> 00:02:34,359
and its own mask,

69
00:02:34,359 --> 00:02:36,843
printed on blank plates from yet another

70
00:02:36,843 --> 00:02:38,401
Japanese specialist,

71
00:02:38,401 --> 00:02:39,227
Hoya.

72
00:02:39,437 --> 00:02:40,810
The smaller the chip,

73
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:43,505
the more of these materials it eats.

74
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:46,150
Let me draw why a tiny market

75
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:48,350
can hold so much power.

76
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:50,423
The machine that prints the chip is

77
00:02:50,423 --> 00:02:53,130
worth hundreds of millions of dollars.

78
00:02:53,210 --> 00:02:55,104
The resist on a wafer costs very

79
00:02:55,104 --> 00:02:57,030
little by comparison.

80
00:02:57,210 --> 00:02:59,510
But the factory needs both.

81
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:01,485
If either one is missing,

82
00:03:01,485 --> 00:03:03,310
the whole line stops.

83
00:03:03,370 --> 00:03:06,040
So the cheapest ingredient can carry the

84
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:09,310
same power as the most expensive machine.

85
00:03:09,550 --> 00:03:11,625
In twenty nineteen,

86
00:03:11,625 --> 00:03:15,533
one country tested exactly that idea.

87
00:03:21,183 --> 00:03:24,255
What happens when a supplier closes the

88
00:03:24,255 --> 00:03:25,162
tap?

89
00:03:30,183 --> 00:03:31,321
On July first,

90
00:03:31,321 --> 00:03:32,690
twenty nineteen,

91
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:35,476
in a decades-old dispute with South Korea

92
00:03:35,476 --> 00:03:37,542
over wartime forced labour,

93
00:03:37,542 --> 00:03:40,096
Japan announced it would restrict exports

94
00:03:40,096 --> 00:03:42,553
of three materials to Korea.

95
00:03:42,903 --> 00:03:44,795
Fluorinated polyimide,

96
00:03:44,795 --> 00:03:46,493
used in phone screens.

97
00:03:46,493 --> 00:03:47,933
Photoresist.

98
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:50,555
And ultra-pure hydrogen fluoride,

99
00:03:50,555 --> 00:03:53,273
used to clean and etch wafers.

100
00:03:53,623 --> 00:03:55,719
Korea is home to two of the

101
00:03:55,719 --> 00:03:58,051
world's biggest memory makers,

102
00:03:58,051 --> 00:04:00,223
Samsung and SK hynix.

103
00:04:00,383 --> 00:04:01,711
And Japan supplied,

104
00:04:01,711 --> 00:04:03,039
by one estimate,

105
00:04:03,039 --> 00:04:05,515
about seventy percent or more of these

106
00:04:05,515 --> 00:04:07,915
materials to the whole world.

107
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:10,480
Korea scrambled.

108
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,640
Samsung stepped up testing of resists and

109
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:14,820
hydrogen fluoride from other suppliers.

110
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:17,331
A Korean chemical maker,

111
00:04:17,331 --> 00:04:18,150
Soulbrain,

112
00:04:18,150 --> 00:04:20,971
raced to match the purity of the

113
00:04:20,971 --> 00:04:22,700
Japanese gas.

114
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:24,723
Shipments from Japan now needed

115
00:04:24,723 --> 00:04:26,980
case-by-case permission.

116
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,249
For the first time,

117
00:04:28,249 --> 00:04:30,390
the chip industry saw a supply of

118
00:04:30,390 --> 00:04:33,131
chemicals turned into a lever.

119
00:04:33,383 --> 00:04:35,643
Did Korea break free?

120
00:04:35,643 --> 00:04:36,673
Partly.

121
00:04:36,873 --> 00:04:39,159
According to Korean industry reports,

122
00:04:39,159 --> 00:04:41,272
it now makes more of the ordinary

123
00:04:41,272 --> 00:04:42,833
materials at home.

124
00:04:43,123 --> 00:04:45,172
But for the most advanced chips,

125
00:04:45,172 --> 00:04:46,923
the pattern repeats.

126
00:04:46,993 --> 00:04:48,398
The finer the circuits,

127
00:04:48,398 --> 00:04:50,435
the more Korea depends on Japanese

128
00:04:50,435 --> 00:04:52,053
materials again.

129
00:04:52,273 --> 00:04:55,101
Every new generation of chips moves the

130
00:04:55,101 --> 00:04:56,353
finish line.

131
00:04:56,617 --> 00:05:00,067
A chemical can be restricted.

132
00:05:00,127 --> 00:05:03,861
A gas can simply disappear.

133
00:05:09,517 --> 00:05:12,326
Why would a war in Ukraine threaten

134
00:05:12,326 --> 00:05:15,110
chip factories in Taiwan?

135
00:05:18,517 --> 00:05:20,347
Because of neon.

136
00:05:20,407 --> 00:05:23,028
Chipmakers use ultra-pure neon gas inside

137
00:05:23,028 --> 00:05:26,487
the lasers of their lithography machines.

138
00:05:26,617 --> 00:05:28,955
And in early twenty twenty-two,

139
00:05:28,955 --> 00:05:30,820
two Ukrainian companies,

140
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:33,866
Ingas in Mariupol and Cryoin in Odessa,

141
00:05:33,866 --> 00:05:34,787
produced,

142
00:05:34,787 --> 00:05:36,653
by Reuters' calculation,

143
00:05:36,653 --> 00:05:39,250
forty-five to fifty-four percent of the

144
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:41,267
world's neon for chipmaking.

145
00:05:41,387 --> 00:05:43,181
When Russia invaded,

146
00:05:43,181 --> 00:05:44,561
both shut down.

147
00:05:44,817 --> 00:05:46,587
Why Ukraine?

148
00:05:46,657 --> 00:05:49,357
Because neon is a by-product.

149
00:05:49,647 --> 00:05:52,015
It is collected from steelmaking,

150
00:05:52,015 --> 00:05:55,364
and historically up to ninety percent of

151
00:05:55,364 --> 00:05:57,517
the neon for the chip industry came

152
00:05:57,517 --> 00:06:00,124
as a by-product of Russian steel plants,

153
00:06:00,124 --> 00:06:02,994
with companies in Ukraine turning it into

154
00:06:02,994 --> 00:06:05,747
the ultra-pure gas chipmakers need.

155
00:06:06,057 --> 00:06:08,698
The whole chip industry used about about

156
00:06:08,698 --> 00:06:10,526
five hundred and forty tons of it

157
00:06:10,526 --> 00:06:12,141
in twenty twenty-one.

158
00:06:12,383 --> 00:06:15,043
The big chipmakers survived.

159
00:06:15,183 --> 00:06:17,252
They had learned from an earlier scare

160
00:06:17,252 --> 00:06:18,608
in twenty fourteen,

161
00:06:18,608 --> 00:06:20,654
when Russia annexed Crimea,

162
00:06:20,654 --> 00:06:22,633
and kept safety stocks.

163
00:06:22,843 --> 00:06:25,593
But replacing the lost supply was slow.

164
00:06:25,693 --> 00:06:28,343
Building new neon purification lines

165
00:06:28,343 --> 00:06:30,512
elsewhere could take nine months to two

166
00:06:30,512 --> 00:06:31,353
years.

167
00:06:31,553 --> 00:06:33,685
Neon showed that a chokepoint does not

168
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:36,203
need a government to switch it off.

169
00:06:36,293 --> 00:06:38,335
A war is enough.

170
00:06:38,583 --> 00:06:39,291
In fact,

171
00:06:39,291 --> 00:06:41,707
after the scare of twenty fourteen,

172
00:06:41,707 --> 00:06:44,635
the industry had already started to spread

173
00:06:44,635 --> 00:06:45,723
its bets.

174
00:06:45,913 --> 00:06:48,639
By one consultant's estimate at Bain,

175
00:06:48,639 --> 00:06:51,391
only about two-fifths of the neon used

176
00:06:51,391 --> 00:06:53,392
for chips still came from Russia and

177
00:06:53,392 --> 00:06:56,493
Ukraine by the time of the invasion.

178
00:06:56,643 --> 00:06:58,833
The lesson had been learned once.

179
00:06:58,833 --> 00:07:00,909
It had to be learned again.

180
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:02,939
And then came the metal,

181
00:07:02,939 --> 00:07:05,791
controlled by the country that wanted it

182
00:07:05,791 --> 00:07:07,168
controlled.

183
00:07:12,817 --> 00:07:15,531
What happens when one country produces

184
00:07:15,531 --> 00:07:18,030
almost all of something?

185
00:07:21,817 --> 00:07:22,787
Meet gallium,

186
00:07:22,787 --> 00:07:25,522
a soft silver metal used in special

187
00:07:25,522 --> 00:07:27,238
chips for defense systems,

188
00:07:27,238 --> 00:07:29,497
telecom equipment and LEDs.

189
00:07:29,497 --> 00:07:31,739
In the United States,

190
00:07:31,739 --> 00:07:34,010
chips use about four in five of

191
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:36,597
all the gallium consumed.

192
00:07:36,747 --> 00:07:39,624
And according to the US Geological Survey,

193
00:07:39,624 --> 00:07:42,314
China produced ninety-nine percent of the

194
00:07:42,314 --> 00:07:44,983
world's raw gallium in twenty twenty-four.

195
00:07:45,217 --> 00:07:47,166
In August twenty twenty-three,

196
00:07:47,166 --> 00:07:50,231
China began requiring licences for every

197
00:07:50,231 --> 00:07:51,657
gallium export.

198
00:07:51,657 --> 00:07:53,197
Prices jumped.

199
00:07:53,197 --> 00:07:55,301
Raw gallium in China went from about

200
00:07:55,301 --> 00:07:57,826
two hundred and forty dollars a kilogram

201
00:07:57,826 --> 00:08:00,141
in mid twenty twenty-three to four hundred

202
00:08:00,141 --> 00:08:02,456
and twenty dollars by October twenty

203
00:08:02,456 --> 00:08:03,687
twenty-four.

204
00:08:03,767 --> 00:08:04,159
Then,

205
00:08:04,159 --> 00:08:06,200
in December twenty twenty-four,

206
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:08,880
China banned gallium exports to the United

207
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,717
States altogether.

208
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:12,100
A year later,

209
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,682
after talks between the American and

210
00:08:14,682 --> 00:08:16,067
Chinese presidents,

211
00:08:16,067 --> 00:08:18,310
China suspended that ban.

212
00:08:18,410 --> 00:08:20,290
But it only paused it.

213
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:22,756
Exporters still need a licence from

214
00:08:22,756 --> 00:08:24,968
